04" :question/id #uuid "84116a53-1342-5c6b-abeb-dda206837ef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-95004" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t+{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=3-t-3{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =2\\cdot (2t+{t}^{3})+2\\cdot (3-t-3{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =4t+2{t}^{3}+6-2t-6{t}^{3} \\\\  & =6+2t-4{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95004/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95004"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106738/selection/2625f37ecdbfc5e6d93366aaabe7f468e7333c6a443c66cb8d193bdb9e920b57" :answer/id #uuid "02e7ecbb-8dda-5f74-95b0-670832ecbc8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106738/selection/c20a1298460845cfea5fc339e24c77043b706d25c0add662859b5a32c630e69b" :answer/id #uuid "3508ff3e-9a54-59c3-9029-4361f334ca00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106738/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5" :answer/id #uuid "61ac3570-5917-5024-b31f-df37e093b893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106738/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73