{t}^{2}+t)+{x}_{2}({t}^{2}-2t+4)+{x}_{3}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-2) & =2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3} \\\\ (4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})t+({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+{x}_{3}{t}^{3} & =2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{4}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n4{x}_{2}-2\\cdot 1=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{1}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-106835/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106835"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95030/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "7bd9a18a-7609-5002-bc53-17908ef0e765" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95030/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "0345acee-6e41-54ee-b14b-a61bb205ee9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95030/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "8022aefe-4682-52e0-8235-99a02c080319" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95030/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0a54e637-064a-5845-abe5-8dc53ac277ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95030/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "e6bd710b-e32d-5fa6-8592-a94ea9592a67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95030/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b32bd0f3-66e4-5dac-b2f1-148d081ef694" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95030/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-95030/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-95030/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-95030/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-95030/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-95030/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95030" :question/id #uuid "1676a3ff-fcb1-5054-9d57-868a55967c3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95030" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}+t-2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}+3t-6,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=-2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2},\\,\\,q(t)=-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{t}^{2}+t-2)+{x}_{2}({t}^{2}+3t-6)+{x}_{3}(-2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}) & =-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}{t}^{3}+(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+({x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})t+(-2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}) & =-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-5{x}_{2}+3\\cdot 1=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 1=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{2}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-95030/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95030"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95023/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "432c972d-a34d-5ad7-87ed-923cbb136266" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95023/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "70c9b3a0-4b4a-571c-a226-40141eee0344" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95023/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a42cacb6-31ee-505b-943b-1e4537622faf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95023/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d46cb614-c679-53d3-905c-80b50fd55a9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95023/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "5dc9f2c4-da0a-53ff-86e9-2a375d1dba52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95023/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8301840e-7f8b-5d52-a6b5-5b10da290368" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95023/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-95023/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-95023/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-95023/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-95023/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-95023/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95023" :question/id #uuid "fcdc7d3c-69b8-5cef-bcd7-6562e616e04a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95023" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+t)+{x}_{2}(1-{t}^{2}) & =2+3t+4{t}^{2} \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{1}t-{x}_{2}{t}^{2} & =2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}=3 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-4)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95023/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95023"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8273"] :question/problem "Consider the polynomials $p_1(t)$ and $p_2(t),$ given by\n\n$$\np_1(t)=3+2t, \\qquad\n\tp_2(t)=-t+t^2.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $\\mathcal{B}=\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/3274a690fa59f7d7368fcbe54004eab244c9845e20bf03ffce1e9fa25bbaf4bc.png)" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/170acd827e8b97471869159c5d9af88b0e4324b25ca1b42ec652011ece6a5174.png)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =4\\cdot (3+2t)+(-3)\\cdot (-t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12+8t+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =12+11t-3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8274"] :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/8a495251bb5d61eab1568624a6e1c213ccee49ec98fc8d5ff5c17fc841d027bf.png)\nIf $\\mathcal B = \\{B_1,B_2\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ B_1, B_2 \\},$ calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/342997674c65cf5c4d14f0b2a7df2649bf99a8b0c003be93efa983f317faa7a1.png)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 B_1 +x_2 B_2 = A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/ebd814bcb627ef3b9208bc0960bdaf48b9448396ed7e95d18d8c4abbf1169244.png)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 18 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=18 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get $x_2 =9.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-9 & =-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/dfc845ca1739c329e5636726466c76efee7eba19df4adc0909110506f894e72d.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8275"] :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\np_1(t)=5+t^2, \\quad\np_2(t)=3t-2t^2, \\quad\nq(t)=5-3t+3t^2.\n$$\n\nIf $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\},$ find $[q(t)]_{\\mathcal{B}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 p_1(t)+x_2 p_2(t) = q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(5+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(3t-2{t}^{2}) & =5-3t+3{t}^{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =5-3t+3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/195a50f130cc40c4a725066035f2da3ef25b725df96601e53f70716bd82b4f4a.png)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{5}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get $x_1=1$ and $x_2 =-1.$ Therefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/9f23f71e833d7a7f81f511e1dfb72861ed753cb514de43d6cabfeb3c6b65fadb.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
